---
import { hackingPrizePost } from '../../../data/blog'
import ArticleLayout from '../../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro'
---

<ArticleLayout {...hackingPrizePost} eyebrow="The Authier hacking prize">
  <p>
    A password manager earns trust by standing up to scrutiny. Today, we are
    putting a reward behind that idea: <strong>hack Authier and receive 10 LTC
    (Litecoin)</strong>. The challenge is specific: fully decrypt a user's stored
    vault secrets and demonstrate the attack programmatically.
  </p>

  <aside class="prize-card" aria-label="Hacking prize requirements">
    <p class="prize-label">The reward</p>
    <p class="prize-amount">10 <span>LTC</span></p>
    <p class="prize-requirement">
      Full decryption of stored secrets.<br />
      Reproducible, programmatic proof.
    </p>
    <a href="mailto:security@authier.pm">Submit to security@authier.pm →</a>
  </aside>

  <h2>What counts as a successful hack?</h2>
  <p>
    A qualifying submission must show a vulnerability in Authier that lets an
    attacker recover the complete plaintext secrets in a user's vault without
    the user's master password, legitimate decryption keys, or normal authorized
    unlock. That includes the secret values stored in the test vault, such as
    passwords and TOTP seeds, rather than only item titles or account metadata.
  </p>
  <p>
    Getting a copy of encrypted data, bypassing a login screen, or showing a
    screenshot of a claimed compromise does not by itself meet this challenge.
    The result must be <strong>full decryption of stored secrets</strong>, with
    working code that demonstrates how the attacker gets there.
  </p>

  <h2>Show it in code</h2>
  <p>
    Send a runnable proof of concept that we can reproduce independently. A
    script, automated test, or small program is welcome. Include:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>The setup:</strong> the affected Authier version or commit,
      platform, dependencies, and any access the attacker needs to start.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The attack:</strong> complete source code and exact commands to
      run it, from the starting conditions through decryption.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The result:</strong> a test vault containing synthetic secrets,
      with output showing that the program recovered every stored secret
      correctly. Keep the master password and legitimate decryption keys out of
      the attack's inputs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The explanation:</strong> the flaw the program exploits and why
      it compromises Authier's protection of stored secrets.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    We will review the report, reproduce the demonstration, and pay the
    <strong>10 LTC reward</strong> for a qualifying, verified full-decryption
    attack. The reward is denominated in Litecoin.
  </p>

  <h2>Research with accounts you control</h2>
  <p>
    Use your own test accounts and synthetic secrets, or accounts whose owners
    have explicitly permitted the test. You do not need to expose anyone's real
    passwords to prove that Authier's protections can be broken. Do not access
    other users' data, disrupt the service, or use phishing or social engineering.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our <a href="https://github.com/authier-pm/authier/blob/main/SECURITY.md">vulnerability
    disclosure policy</a> describes the supported versions, scope, and research
    exclusions. Share findings privately and give us time to investigate and
    address them before public disclosure. Other security reports are welcome
    at the same address, even when they do not meet this prize's full-decryption
    requirement.
  </p>

  <h2>Send your submission</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:security@authier.pm">security@authier.pm</a> with the
    subject <strong>Authier 10 LTC challenge</strong>, your reproduction
    instructions, and the proof-of-concept source attached or linked privately.
    Use synthetic data in the report. If you want to encrypt your submission,
    the disclosure policy includes our PGP key identifier.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ready to inspect the implementation? Start with the
    <a href="/security">security architecture</a> and the
    <a href="https://github.com/authier-pm/authier">open-source repository</a>.
    We look forward to seeing what you find.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
  .prize-card {
    margin: 38px 0 48px;
    padding: clamp(26px, 5vw, 42px);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: 18px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0, rgba(105, 230, 204, 0.13), transparent 65%),
      var(--surface);
  }

  .prize-card .prize-label {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .prize-card .prize-amount {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 12vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 670;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .prize-amount span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.55em;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .prize-card .prize-requirement {
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prize-card a {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
</style>
